  "historical_output_text": " Here's what works to solve a creak on stairs in an older wooden-framing structure - First identify what component of stairs the cack sounds like to emanated - Is a step caking or a rail? If a single component, you need to adjust the caking surface, such as a piece a trim or tread to be parallel with adjacent stairs - This usually entails shoving a shim in-between components until parallel, and screw in place to ensure that it is held - This is not as easy on old homes because you will probably have a gap, which can be addressed using an adjustable shim. Once that piece has moved and become flush - the step will become stable, the shim will ensure you don\nThe other scenario where there may just a gap in-between the component that may be creating a loud sound and that may also just require shoving",
